.TH SESSION-REPORT 1 "2026-10-14" "SASD Freeware" "Unix Administration"
.SH NAME
session-report \- read-only inventory of current interactive user sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B session-report
[--user NAME] [--input FILE] [--null]
.br
.B session-report
--help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads current interactive login sessions from the system who command.
Outputs USER, TTY and unmodified date/origin DETAILS plus counts. These
fields are OS-specific and do not constitute an authentication history.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --user NAME
Include only sessions for this user.
.TP
.B --input FILE
Parse saved who output from an existing regular file, refusing symlinks.
.TP
.B --null
Output three raw NUL-terminated fields per row, no header or totals.
.TP
.B --help, --version
Show usage or version without invoking who.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 completed, 1 malformed input records, 2 usage, 3 unavailable input/backend.
.SH SECURITY
Read only. Session and host details can be sensitive. No root required.
.SH SEE ALSO
who(1), last(1), ps(1), process-report(1)
